* WORKSPACE ADDITIVE OPEN and SCOPED SAVE -- R128 (owner, 2026-08-26).
* Explicit-run until soaked. Self-bootstrapping in SANDBOX, self-erasing.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOA
ERASE WAOT1 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 WAOT1 (ID N(4), MARK C(8))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "AAA"
CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOB
ERASE WAOT2 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 WAOT2 (ID N(4), MARK C(8))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "BBB"
CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOC
ERASE WAOT3 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 WAOT3 (ID N(4), MARK C(8))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "CCC"
CLOSE
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
* GUARDS. Each fixture read ON ITS OWN, before any of them is opened as a
* workspace. Without these an arm reading the wrong MARK cannot tell a broken
* verb from a table that never carried the value.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOA
USE WAOT1
? "WAO_G0_fixture_a_reads_AAA:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOB
USE WAOT2
? "WAO_G1_fixture_b_reads_BBB:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOC
USE WAOT3
? "WAO_G2_fixture_c_reads_CCC:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "CCC")
CLOSE
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
SET PATH DBF DBF
* T1/T2 -- ADDITIVE OPEN. T1 asks the answerable question: after opening WAOA
* and then WAOB, does AREA 0 STILL HOLD WAOA'S TABLE. Under the replacing OPEN
* it holds WAOB's, so this reads .F. rather than printing nothing.
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF/SANDBOX/WAOA
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF/SANDBOX/WAOB
SELECT 0
? "WAO_T1_first_workspace_survived_the_second_open:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
SELECT 1
? "WAO_T2_second_workspace_landed_beside_it:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
* T3/T4 -- RE-ENTRY adds only what is not already open. T3 is green under BOTH
* implementations and is NOT a discriminator; it is here because a re-entry
* that disturbed the surviving area would show up nowhere else.
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF/SANDBOX/WAOA
SELECT 0
? "WAO_T3_reentry_left_the_open_table_alone:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
SELECT 1
? "WAO_T4_reentry_spared_the_other_workspace:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
* T5 -- SCOPED SAVE, asserted by WHERE THE NEXT AREA LANDS rather than by
* counting what is absent. IT BUILDS ITS TWO WORKSPACES WITH NEW AND ADD, NOT
* WITH OPEN, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT: measured 2026-08-26, a first cut that
* used OPEN read GREEN on both binaries, because under the replacing OPEN the
* second one closes the first and there is never a second populated workspace
* to save from. The additive defect was MASKING the save defect -- which is
* also the reason the save defect was rarely reached in the field. NEW and ADD
* are untouched by R128 and additive on both builds, so this arm tests the
* serializer and nothing else. WAOX is saved while WAOY is also populated; the
* posture should carry ONE area, so the reload leaves slot 1 free and the ADD
* lands there. Under the unscoped sweep the posture carries BOTH, the reload
* fills 0 and 1, the ADD lands at 2, and slot 1 reads BBB.
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
WORKSPACE NEW WAOX
WORKSPACE SWITCH WAOX
WORKSPACE ADD DBF/SANDBOX/WAOA/WAOT1.dbf
WORKSPACE NEW WAOY
WORKSPACE SWITCH WAOY
WORKSPACE ADD DBF/SANDBOX/WAOB/WAOT2.dbf
WORKSPACE SWITCH WAOX
WORKSPACE SAVE waoscope MEMO
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
WORKSPACE LOAD waoscope MEMO
WORKSPACE ADD DBF/SANDBOX/WAOC/WAOT3.dbf
SELECT 1
? "WAO_T5_scoped_save_carried_one_workspace:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "CCC")
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
WORKSPACE DESTROY WAOA
WORKSPACE DESTROY WAOB
WORKSPACE DESTROY WAOX
WORKSPACE DESTROY WAOY
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOA
ERASE WAOT1 CONFIRM
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOB
ERASE WAOT2 CONFIRM
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/WAOC
ERASE WAOT3 CONFIRM
